      "line": 6780,
      "code": "mrb_parser_parse(p, c);",
      "note": "The staged plain-text PoC is parsed into the AST `p->tree`. That AST shape is the first project-side materialization of attacker input that later drives the vulnerable rescue-code generation path.",
      "kind": "source"
    },
    {
      "file": "mrbgems/mruby-compiler/core/codegen.c",
      "function": "genjmp2",
      "line": null,
      "code": "gen_S(s, pc);",
      "note": "In the `a > 0xff` (`OP_EXT1`) branch, `genjmp2()` writes the raw 16-bit `pc` value into the jump-link field instead of calling `gen_jmpdst(s, pc)`. That violates the link-format contract later assumed by `dispatch()` and `dispatch_linked()`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "mrbgems/mruby-compiler/core/codegen.c",
      "function": "genjmp2",
      "line": 448,
      "code": "gen_S(s, pc);",
      "note": "In the `a > 0xff` (`OP_EXT1`) branch, `genjmp2()` writes the raw 16-bit `pc` value into the jump-link field instead of calling `gen_jmpdst(s, pc)`. That violates the link-format contract later assumed by `dispatch()` and `dispatch_linked()`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_line"
    },
    {
      "file": "mrbgems/mruby-compiler/core/codegen.c",
      "function": "dispatch",
      "line": null,
      "code": "newpos = (int16_t)PEEK_S(s->iseq+pos0);",
      "note": "A later `dispatch()` iteration reads the next 16-bit jump-link field from an out-of-range `pos0`, so `PEEK_S` dereferences past the allocated bytecode buffer `s->iseq`. Stage 01 ASan reports the crash here as a 1-byte heap-buffer-overflow read.",
      "kind": "sink_function"
    },
    {
      "file": "mrbgems/mruby-compiler/core/codegen.c",
      "function": "dispatch",
      "line": 573,
      "code": "newpos = (int16_t)PEEK_S(s->iseq+pos0);",
